course: dictionary
lesson: 11849
title: Blurred
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Blurred means not clear or sharp. When something is blurred, its edges and details are hard to see. Read the words around it to find its meaning. «The photo was blurred because Sam moved the camera.» The camera moved, so the picture is not sharp. Blurred means not clear.
explain: Blurred can also describe memories or lines. «Her memories of the holiday were blurred after so many years.» Years have passed, so she cannot remember the details clearly. «The line between fair and unfair had blurred.» When two things are blurred together, they are hard to tell apart.
explain: Blurred vision means you cannot see clearly. «After the bump on the head, Ella's vision went blurred.» This is a warning sign, so tell an adult straight away. Always check the clues in the sentence, then try your meaning in its place to see if it still makes sense.
fact: Blurred means not clear or sharp.
fact: Blur means to become unclear, or to make something unclear. Blurred is its past form.
fact: «Blurred» can describe a photo, a memory, or a line that is no longer clearly separated.
fact: Blurred vision can be a warning sign, especially after a bump on the head. Tell an adult straight away.
fact: Tears, movement, or speed can all make things look blurred.
exercise: «The photo was blurred because Sam moved the camera.» What does blurred mean here? | Bright and colourful | *Not clear or sharp | Printed in black and white | Very small
exercise: «Her memories of the holiday were blurred after so many years.» What are blurred memories? | Easy to remember word for word | *Hard to remember clearly | Written down in a diary | Very happy and exciting
exercise: «The sharp photo was clear, but the other one was blurred.» Find and copy the word that means the opposite of blurred. | one | other | *clear | photo
test: «After the match, the line between fair and unfair had blurred.» Here blurred means? | Finished quickly | Painted in bright colours | *Become unclear and hard to tell apart | Written in capital letters
test: Ella says her vision went blurred after she bumped her head. What should she do? | Keep playing and wait to see if it passes | Rub her eyes and keep reading | Ignore it, because it is only a small bump | *Tell an adult straight away
exam: Which word is the past form of blur? | blurring | *blurred | blur | blurs
